    <string name="manufacturer_whitelist_title">Manufacturer Background Optimization</string>
    <string name="manufacturer_whitelist_message">Different manufacturers have different restrictions on background apps. To ensure TTS Server can run continuously in the background, please add this app to the following whitelists:\n\n1. Battery optimization whitelist\n2. Background running whitelist\n3. Auto start management\n\nClick OK to jump to system settings.</string>
    <string name="keep_alive_help_message"><![CDATA[<b>Why Keep Alive?</b><br/><br/>Android automatically cleans up background apps to save battery. Manufacturers (Xiaomi, Huawei, OPPO, vivo, etc.) have additional restrictions that may kill TTS Server.<br/><br/><b>Recommended Setup</b><br/><br/>Basic users: Enable "Battery Whitelist" only<br/>Need stability: Whitelist + Keep Alive Service<br/>Maximum keep-alive: Enable multiple advanced options<br/><br/><b>Keep-Alive Options</b><br/><br/><b>Battery Whitelist</b><br/>System feature to bypass battery optimization. Essential.<br/><br/><b>Keep Alive Service</b><br/>Foreground service + wake lock. Recommended baseline.<br/><br/><b>Boot Auto Start</b><br/>Automatically start service after device reboot.<br/><br/><b>Accessibility Keep Alive</b><br/>Highest system priority, most stable. Requires manual permission.<br/><br/><b>Notification Keep Alive</b><br/>Use notification listener service. Requires manual permission.<br/><br/><b>Alarm Keep Alive</b><br/>Wake up every minute. Higher battery usage.<br/><br/><b>Network Keep Alive</b><br/>Keep network connection active. Useful for forwarder.<br/><br/><b>Pixel Keep Alive</b><br/>1-pixel window when screen off, auto-hides when on. Zero disturbance.<br/><br/><b>Notes</b><br/><br/>1. Keep-alive merges with forwarder notification when running<br/>2. Some manufacturers need extra "Manufacturer Settings"<br/>3. Multiple options increase battery usage<br/>4. TTS engine mode does not occupy audio focus]]></string>
